    {
      "id": "claim_536bb4ec7e714e93bcd2cb95f9359445",
      "statement": "_handle_precommit_failure implements the self-healing loop: it increments metadata[precommit_retries] and, within ZEROFACTORY_MAX_PRECOMMIT_RETRIES (default 3), routes the task back to zf-builder as a claimable todo retry (clearing awaiting_pr) with the exact failing output injected into the respawned worker's prompt; once retries are exhausted the first exhaustion stamps triage_phase='recovery' and routes the task to zf-orchestrator for one autonomous diagnostic attempt (gated on orchestrator_recovery_count < 1), and a second exhaustion moves the task to blocked with blocked_reason_type='stuck' and assignee 'human' for inspection and posts a failure comment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://dispatcher/worktree.py#L1127-L1269",
