    {
      "id": "claim_7414caddf45c4549ae10dc50ac6b83c1",
      "statement": "reaper.py detects hung workers using a shared _compute_stuck_state (per-task max running time plus inactivity timeout) so reap_active_workers (the only path that kills processes) and check_stuck_tasks (reporting/manual reap) cannot drift apart; reaper DB connections are WAL-tolerant (PRAGMA busy_timeout) and reap_stuck_tasks retries on sqlite3.OperationalError 'database is locked' with capped backoff; worker-failure handling is retry-oriented (a failed or vanished running worker returns to todo for re-spawn up to DEFAULT_MAX_WORKER_RETRIES), and on exhaustion with assignee != zf-orchestrator and orchestrator_recovery_count < 1 the task is routed back to todo with triage_phase='recovery' for one autonomous attempt, while a second exhaustion stamps permanently_blocked with blocked_reason_type='stuck' and assignee 'human'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://dispatcher/reaper.py#L151-L674",
